---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy — ${site.name}`}
  description={`How ${site.name} handles your data. No third-party analytics, no advertising, no cross-site tracking.`}
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="page">
    <header class="page-head container reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p>
        Short version: <strong>no third-party analytics, no advertising, and no
        cross-site tracking</strong>. We count page views ourselves, without
        cookies and without storing your IP address, and otherwise process only
        the minimum needed to serve the site and to reply if you contact us.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {site.privacyUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="container prose reveal">
      <section>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          This website (<strong>liveolator.zalmanim.com</strong>) is operated by
          {site.operator}, which acts as the data controller for the limited
          personal data described here. For any privacy question or request,
          contact <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What we collect, why, and on what basis</h2>
        <p>We keep this deliberately small:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Server &amp; CDN logs.</strong> Like almost every website, our
            server and content-delivery network record technical request data —
            your IP address, browser/user-agent, the time, and the page requested.
            <em>Purpose:</em> to serve the site, keep it secure, and prevent abuse.
            <em>Legal basis:</em> our legitimate interest (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)) in
            operating a secure service. These logs are kept only for a short period
            and then deleted or rotated.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Messages you send us.</strong> The feedback form simply opens
            your own email app with a pre-filled message — it is <em>not</em>
            submitted to or stored by this website. If you choose to send it, we
            receive whatever you include (typically your name, email address and
            message). <em>Purpose:</em> to read and respond to your inquiry or
            suggestion. <em>Legal basis:</em> our legitimate interest in handling
            correspondence, and taking steps at your request. We keep these emails
            only as long as needed to deal with your message.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Aggregate page counts.</strong> If your browser runs
            JavaScript, each page you open reports its own address and the site
            that linked you to our own server at zalmanim.com — no third party, no
            advertising network, and <em>no cookie</em>. Your IP address is
            <em>not</em> stored: it is combined with your browser string and a
            secret that is thrown away and regenerated every day, and only the
            resulting hash is kept, so two visits on the same day can be told
            apart without anyone knowing whose they were. Once the day turns, even
            that link is gone. We also keep a coarse country (from Cloudflare) and
            whether you were on a phone or a desktop. <em>Purpose:</em> to know
            which pages people actually use. <em>Legal basis:</em> our legitimate
            interest in basic, privacy-preserving usage figures. To switch it off
            for your browser, open any page of this site with
            <code>?zbi=off</code> at the end of the address.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Beyond that aggregate count, we do <strong>not</strong> use third-party
          analytics, advertising, profiling, or tracking that follows you between
          sites, and we do not sell or share your data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          We set <strong>no cookies for analytics or advertising</strong>, so this
          site does not ask for cookie consent. Our network provider (Cloudflare)
          may set strictly-necessary security cookies to protect the site from
          attacks; these are exempt from consent and are not used to track you.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you <strong>open the support chat and send a message</strong>, one
          functional cookie is set so the same panel can show you the reply when
          you come back. It identifies the conversation, not you: it holds a
          random token, it is readable only by the server, and it is the reason
          you do not have to leave an email address to get an answer. Nothing is
          set if you never open the chat.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Service providers</h2>
        <p>
          We rely on a few processors to run the site. Each may process technical
          data (such as your IP address) only to provide their service:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Hostinger</strong> — hosting for the server that serves this site.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — DNS, CDN and security proxy; processes requests, including IP addresses, at its global edge.</li>
          <li><strong>Google (Gmail)</strong> — receives and stores the emails you choose to send us.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Some of these providers may process data outside your country, including
          outside the EU/EEA, under appropriate safeguards such as the European
          Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          If you are in the EU/EEA (or a region with similar laws) you have the
          right to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to the processing of
          your personal data, and to data portability. To exercise any of these,
          email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> and
          we'll respond. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with your
          local data-protection supervisory authority.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>This site is not directed at children and we don't knowingly collect their data.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy as the site evolves. The date at the top
          reflects the latest revision.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back to home</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 40px; }
  .page-head { max-width: 760px; padding-top: 36px; }
  .page-head h1 { font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 52px); }
  .page-head p { margin-top: 16px; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 18px; }
  .page-head strong { color: var(--text); }
  .updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px !important;
    color: var(--text-mute) !important;
    margin-top: 12px !important;
  }

  .prose { max-width: 720px; padding-bottom: 24px; }
  .prose section { margin-top: 34px; }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    padding-bottom: 9px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .prose p {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 16.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .prose ul {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    padding-left: 22px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .prose li {
    color: var(--text-dim);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .prose li::marker { color: var(--amber-dim); }
  .prose strong { color: var(--text); }
  .prose em { color: var(--text-dim); font-style: normal; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .back { margin-top: 40px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 14px; }
</style>
